creating a SageMaker User Profile 👤.

1. User profile → Name

You enter the name for the SageMaker user.

Example:

sugumar-sagemaker-profile

This profile represents a user who will work inside the SageMaker Domain.

====

2. Execution role 🔐

You must select an IAM Role.

The Execution role gives SageMaker permission to access AWS resources on your behalf.

For example:

SageMaker User
      ↓
User Profile 👤
      ↓
Execution Role 🔐
      ↓
S3 🪣 | SageMaker 🧠 | Other AWS Resources

Example role shown in your screenshot:

AmazonSageMaker-ExecutionRole...

This role allows SageMaker to perform tasks such as:

Access data from S3
Train ML models
Save model outputs
Run SageMaker notebooks/apps

====

3. Create role using the role creation wizard

If you don't already have an IAM role, click:

Create role using the role creation wizard

AWS will help create the required permissions.

====

4. Tags — optional 🏷️

Tags are labels used to organize AWS resources.

Example:

Project = AI Learning
User = Sugumar

Tags are optional, so you can skip them while learning.

===


Simple flow
SageMaker Domain 🏢
        ↓
Create User Profile 👤
        ↓
Give a Name
        ↓
Attach Execution Role 🔐
        ↓
User can access SageMaker resources 🧠

Most important field here is the Execution role, because without proper permissions, the SageMaker user cannot access resources like S3 or run certain SageMaker tasks.

====

